[?2004hroot@dc0cce53cd86:/task/work# cat > /task/output/METHODS.md << 'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> # IMM-FC-012 PBMC lineage panel - analysis notes
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 0. State of the raw files
[?2004l[?2004h> * FCS 3.1, list-mode, 12 parameters (FSC-A, FSC-H, SSC-A, 8 fluorescence areas, Time), `$MODE=L`.
[?2004l[?2004h> * Detector voltages are stored per parameter in `$PnV`.
[?2004l[?2004h> * The event data are **uncompensated** (single-stain tubes show their full spillover), even though every file
[?2004l[?2004h>   carries `APPLY COMPENSATION = TRUE` and a `$SPILLOVER` keyword.
[?2004l[?2004h> * The `$SPILLOVER` keyword is **identical in all 19 files** and is therefore *not* the matrix that describes
[?2004l[?2004h>   each individual file: it lists PerCP-Cy5.5 -> YG780-A = 0.093, which matches neither the bead tube
[?2004l[?2004h>   (0.152) nor the lot-corrected cell tube (0.253), and it does not change between the 641 V and the 703 V
[?2004l[?2004h>   acquisitions. It was ignored; every matrix below was recomputed from the control tubes.
[?2004l[?2004h>   Cross-check: regressing the raw YG780-A signal of the HLA-DR FMO tubes (which contain every reagent except
[?2004l[?2004h>   PE-Cy7) on the compensated fluorochrome signals gives PerCP-Cy5.5 -> YG780-A = 0.252 (641 V tube) and
[?2004l[?2004h>   0.476 (703 V tube), i.e. the control-derived values, not the keyword values.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Spillover matrices (`spillover.csv`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Row *f*, column *d* = (mean signal of the f-positive control population in d) - (mean of the f-negative
[?2004l[?2004h> population in d), divided by the same difference in f's primary detector, background-free, diagonal = 1.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Control selection (`controls.tsv`):
[?2004l[?2004h> * one candidate per fluorochrome was dropped on purpose: `ctrl_PerCPCy55.fcs` is antibody-capture beads of
[?2004l[?2004h>   reagent lot 2807268, while `panel.tsv` uses lot **3066970** for CD8 PerCP-Cy5.5. That lot was acquired on
[?2004l[?2004h>   cells in `ctrl_PerCPCy55_cells.fcs`, which is what the samples contain, so the **cell** tube was used
[?2004l[?2004h>   (spill into YG780-A 0.253 instead of the bead tube's 0.152).
[?2004l[?2004h> * `ctrl_PECy7.fcs` (YG780-A = 641 V) is recorded at the wrong settings for the last two samples; the
[?2004l[?2004h>   rerun tube `ctrl_PECy7_rerun.fcs` (703 V) is lot-identical and was used for those files.
[?2004l[?2004h> * Zombie Aqua was controlled on cells (1:1 live/heat-killed PBMC), all other conjugates on beads.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Voltage groups of the fluorescence detectors (`$PnV`):
[?2004l[?2004h> * group A, YG780-A = 641 V: PBMC_D617, PBMC_D685, PBMC_D735, PBMC_D829;
[?2004l[?2004h> * group B, YG780-A = 703 V: PBMC_D858, PBMC_D960 (D858 additionally has different FSC/SSC voltages, which
[?2004l[?2004h>   does not change the fluorescence spillover).
[?2004l[?2004h> All other fluorescence detectors have identical voltages in both groups.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Group B matrix from the group-A matrix: the signal gain of YG780-A between the two settings was measured
[?2004l[?2004h> from the PE-Cy7 tube pair (positive-minus-negative excess in YG780-A: 30977 at 641 V -> 58681 at 703 V,
[?2004l[?2004h> k = 1.8944; the 703/641 = 1.097 voltage ratio is *not* the signal gain). Every signal recorded in YG780-A
[?2004l[?2004h> is k times larger at 703 V, hence
[?2004l[?2004h> * A_B[f, d!=YG780-A] = A_A[f, d] for f != PE-Cy7,
[?2004l[?2004h> * A_B[f, YG780-A] = k * A_A[f, YG780-A] for f != PE-Cy7,
[?2004l[?2004h> * A_B[PE-Cy7, d!=YG780-A] = A_A[PE-Cy7, d]/k, A_B[PE-Cy7, YG780-A] = 1.
[?2004l[?2004h> The PE-Cy7 row of group B agrees with the directly measured rerun row to <1%.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Compensation and gating (`frequencies.tsv`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Samples and both FMO tubes were compensated with the matrix of their own voltage group, then gated.
[?2004l[?2004h> All gate boundaries were placed automatically in the empty band (or smoothed minimum) between the two
[?2004l[?2004h> populations of the relevant channel, so the counts do not depend on the exact position of the cut.
[?2004l[?2004h> * `cells`   : FSC-A above the debris gap (FSC voltages differ between files, so the cut is found per file).
[?2004l[?2004h> * `singlets`: FSC-H/FSC-A above the gap (empty band 0.72-0.84 in every file).
[?2004l[?2004h> * `live`    : compensated V525-A (Zombie Aqua) below the gap of the singlet population.
[?2004l[?2004h> * `lymphocytes` = live AND SSC-A below the lymphocyte/monocyte gap AND CD14 -; `monocytes` = CD14 +.
[?2004l[?2004h> * `T_cells` = lymphocytes AND CD3 +; `CD4_T` = CD3+ CD4+ CD8-; `CD8_T` = CD3+ CD4- CD8+;
[?2004l[?2004h>   `DP_T` = CD4+ CD8+; `DN_T` = CD4- CD8-; `B_cells` = lymphocytes CD3- CD19+;
[?2004l[?2004h>   `NK_cells` = lymphocytes CD3- CD19- CD56+. CD4/CD8/CD19/CD56 cuts are taken inside T_cells / CD3-
[?2004l[?2004h>   lymphocytes (hierarchical), all in empty bands.
[?2004l[?2004h>   CD4+CD8+DP+DN = T_cells exactly for every sample; lymphocytes+monocytes = live for every sample.
[?2004l[?2004h> * `activated_CD4_T`, `activated_CD8_T`: FMO gate of section 2 of the SOP. The FMO tube was compensated with
[?2004l[?2004h>   the matrix of its own voltage group (fmo_HLADR.fcs, 641 V, for the group-A samples; fmo_HLADR_rerun.fcs,
[?2004l[?2004h>   703 V, for PBMC_D858 and PBMC_D960) and gated identically down to CD4_T and CD8_T; the threshold is the
[?2004l[?2004h>   99th percentile of the compensated YG780-A signal of that population (linear units):
[?2004l[?2004h>   group A: CD4_T 302.0, CD8_T 431.7; group B: CD4_T 599.9, CD8_T 792.9 (ratio 1.98 ~ the k gain factor).
[?2004l[?2004h>   A sample event of P is HLA-DR + if its compensated YG780-A signal is strictly greater than that threshold.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> * `count` = number of events of the sample's FCS file in the population; `percent_of_parent` =
[?2004l[?2004h>   100 x count / parent count (`all_events` = `$TOT` of the file).
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
